# arvo-digest

A digest of explicit bytes, at a width the type names. Not cryptographic.

Two algorithms by name, `Fnv1a` at 32 and 64 bits and `Xxh3` at 64 and 128 bits. Every path has a
`const fn` form that gives the same value as the runtime one, and a digest narrows into
`arvo_bits::Bits<N>` when the width a consumer pins it to is smaller. A switched digest, FNV-1a on
short input and XXH3 from a measured length on, joins once that length is measured.

Input is `arvo_bits::Bytes` and the digest is held in `arvo_bits::Bits`, with FNV-1a's product taken
from `arvo-numeral`, so no host integer is named here. Depends on `arvo-format`, `arvo-numeral`, `arvo-bits`,
notko, and `xxhash-rust` for XXH3 behind the `xxh3` feature, off by default. `no_std`, no allocation.

## Status

Unreleased, at 0.0.0. The source implements what is described here and its tests pass, and the surface
may still change before a first release.
